/* book exam traps: Tolerance is the full band, not the ± value: 25 ± 0.010 mm has a tolerance of 0.020 mm. | Writing the shaft first. ISO always writes the hole first: H7/g6, G7/h6. A capital letter is always the hole. | Minimum clearance uses the smallest hole and the largest shaft; maximum clearance the largest hole and the smallest shaft. Swapping them gives a wrong sign. | Using the basic size itself as D in the tolerance-unit formula. D is the geometric mean of the step (23.24 mm for 18 to 30 mm). | Calling H7/h6 a transition fit because its minimum clearance is zero. It is a clearance fit. */
